1.chmod <mode> <file> Change file permissions
2.chmod u+x <file> Add execute permission for the
owner
3.chmod 644 <file>
Set file permissions to 644
(read/write for owner, read for
group and everyone else)
4.chmod -R g+w <dir> Add write permission for the
group recursively to a directory
5.chown <owner> <file> Change file owner
6.chown -R <owner> <dir> Change directory owner
recursively
7.chown <owner>:<group>
<file> Change file owner and group
chgrp <group> <file> Change file group

